[Start "ruy-lopez-setup 4...Nf6"]

5. d4 { Strikes in the centre at once. The usual move is 5.O-O; 5.d4 opens the game while Black's king is still in the middle, and its ideas are easier to learn. [%cal Gd4e5] } 5... exd4 { Takes the pawn. White does not hurry to win it back. } ( 5... Nxe4 6. O-O { Castles. With the king safe, the rook comes to e1 and the open e-file works for White. } 6... b5 7. Bb3 d5 8. dxe5 Be6 9. c3 { Gives the bishop a retreat on c2 and keeps the centre solid. The pawn on e5 cramps Black. Plan: Nbd2, Bc2 and Qe2, then go after the knight on e4. } ) ( 5... Nxd4 6. Nxd4 exd4 7. e5 { Kicks the knight before taking back the pawn. } 7... Ne4 8. Qxd4 { Wins the pawn back, with the queen in the centre where the knight cannot chase it. } 8... Nc5 9. Nc3 { Develops. White is ahead in development and the pawn on e5 takes squares from Black. } ) ( 5... Be7 6. O-O { If Black now takes on d4, 7.e5 reaches the main line. } ) 6. O-O { Castles before taking the pawn back. The king is safe, and the rook can come to e1, on the file where Black's king still stands. } 6... Be7 { The safe answer: Black gets ready to castle. } ( 6... d6 7. Nxd4 { Takes the pawn back. The knight on c6 cannot take on d4: the bishop on a4 pins it to the king. [%cal Ga4e8] } 7... Bd7 8. Nxc6 Bxc6 9. Bxc6+ bxc6 10. Nc3 { Black's queenside pawns are split, and White develops with a lead. Plan: Qf3 or f4, and use the d5 square. } ) ( 6... Nxe4 7. Re1 { Pins the knight to the king: it cannot move. [%cal Ge1e8] } 7... d5 8. Nxd4 { Wins the pawn back and attacks the knight on c6. } 8... Bd6 9. Nxc6 Bxh2+ { Black hopes to hit White's king. } 10. Kh1 Qh4 11. Rxe4+ { Gives the rook back at once and checks. } 11... dxe4 12. Qd8+ Qxd8 13. Nxd8+ { The bishop on a4 gives check as the knight takes. } 13... Kxd8 14. Kxh2 { The dust has settled: White has two minor pieces for a rook and pawn, the better side of the trade. Plan: develop with Nc3 and Be3 and go after the pawn on e4. } ) 7. e5 { Kicks the knight from f6. } 7... Ne4 { Into the centre. } ( 7... Nd5 8. Nxd4 { Takes the pawn back; material is level. } ) 8. Nxd4 { Wins back the pawn. Material is level and the pawn on e5 gives White space. } 8... O-O { Castles: now the open e-file holds no danger for Black's king, and the knight has c5 to go to. } ( 8... Nxd4 9. Qxd4 Nc5 10. Nc3 { Develops with the queen in the centre. Black has no easy way to hit the pawn on e5. } ) ( 8... Nc5 9. Nf5 { Attacks the bishop on e7 and eyes g7. } ) 9. Nf5 { Attacks the bishop on e7 and eyes g7. [%cal Gf5e7,Gf5g7] } 9... d5 { Supports the knight on e4 and frees the bishop on c8. } 10. Nxe7+ { Takes the bishop that guards Black's dark squares. } 10... Nxe7 11. c3 { Gives the bishop c2, where it hits the knight on e4. The game is level. Plan: Bc2, f3 to chase the knight, Be3 and Nd2, and keep the pawn on e5 for space. } *
